From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-plat: use generic ACPI initialization without SSPM

The DGX Spark exposes NVDA8000/NVDA8001 controllers but its firmware can
report the SSPM mailbox as absent. Selecting the MediaTek power-management
path by controller ID alone then makes every USB probe fail: the required
Power Wrap request returns -ENODEV. USB storage and input never enumerate.

Only select that path when firmware exposes one of the SSPM transport's
ACPI devices. Otherwise keep the generic ACPI xHCI initialization used by
the working unpatched kernel. Check firmware presence, not driver binding,
so a present transport that fails to initialize still produces an error.
Retain the controller's hardware quirks.

Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c
@@ -250,6 +250,15 @@
 		*priv = *priv_match;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * GB10 firmware can expose the same controller IDs with SSPM disabled.
+	 * In that case firmware owns the PHYs; use the generic ACPI xHCI path.
+	 */
+	if (priv && priv->is_mtk_v2 &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("MTKW8400", NULL, -1) &&
+	    !acpi_dev_present("NVDA8400", NULL, -1))
+		priv->is_mtk_v2 = false;
+
 	if (priv && priv->is_mtk_v2) {
 
 		wakeup_irq = platform_get_irq_optional(pdev, 1);
